WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:02.635
Bladesmiths,
congratulations, you've

00:00:02.736 --> 00:00:04.236
made it into the third
round of this competition,

00:00:04.337 --> 00:00:05.972
and now it's time to send
you back to your home

00:00:06.039 --> 00:00:09.541
forges to recreate this
iconic weapon from history.

00:00:09.642 --> 00:00:10.677
That weapon is

00:00:13.513 --> 00:00:16.949
Charlemagne's Joyeuse.

00:00:17.049 --> 00:00:21.254
Today we are pre-testing
Charlemagne Joyeuse.

00:00:21.354 --> 00:00:24.357
The Joyeuse was supposed to be
a sword wielded by Charlemagne.

00:00:24.423 --> 00:00:27.159
And it is your standard sword
that, as you look at it,

00:00:27.226 --> 00:00:29.195
it's quite decorative
because it's a homage

00:00:29.262 --> 00:00:31.464
to the great Charlemagne.

00:00:31.531 --> 00:00:33.299
NARRATOR: Meaning
joyful, the Joyeuse

00:00:33.365 --> 00:00:35.601
is considered one of the
most famous swords in history

00:00:35.702 --> 00:00:38.772
and was the personal
sidearm of King Charlemagne.

00:00:38.838 --> 00:00:40.139
After the fall of
the Roman Empire,

00:00:40.206 --> 00:00:41.908
Charlemagne used
the blade in battle

00:00:42.008 --> 00:00:44.277
to reunite Western Europe.

00:00:44.343 --> 00:00:46.379
Covered in gold jewels
and floral patterns,

00:00:46.479 --> 00:00:48.347
this weapon was light
and deadly and earned

00:00:48.414 --> 00:00:51.684
the reputation as the sword
that conquered Europe.

00:00:51.750 --> 00:00:54.520
Featuring a double edged blade
with a deep central fuller,

00:00:54.587 --> 00:00:57.623
the sword was also rumored
to have magical powers,

00:00:57.724 --> 00:01:01.394
like the ability to shine
brighter than the sun.

00:01:01.461 --> 00:01:03.229
Today, the legendary
sword can be

00:01:03.295 --> 00:01:05.798
seen on display at the Louvre.

00:01:05.865 --> 00:01:07.133
So when we test
a weapon that's

00:01:07.233 --> 00:01:09.135
tied to a historical
figure, I try

00:01:09.202 --> 00:01:12.071
to embody the feeling of who
that historical figure was.

00:01:12.171 --> 00:01:13.072
When did he live?

00:01:13.172 --> 00:01:14.006
How did he fight?

00:01:14.107 --> 00:01:17.310
[music playing]

00:01:18.978 --> 00:01:21.114
So that way, it ties
into the kind of weapon

00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:22.648
that I'm wielding.

00:01:22.715 --> 00:01:24.517
At the same time, it gets
me into character, I guess.

00:01:24.583 --> 00:01:26.653
I try to embody the
spirit of who they were

00:01:26.753 --> 00:01:28.187
and how they fought.

00:01:28.287 --> 00:01:30.823
So we had some weapons like
Genghis Khan or the barbar--

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:34.127
fighting like a barbarian, or
we had General Patton's sword.

00:01:34.194 --> 00:01:38.497
And of course, now we have
Charlemagne's Joyeuse sword.

00:01:38.598 --> 00:01:40.466
[music playing]

00:01:40.533 --> 00:01:42.101
So with this
particular weapon, we

00:01:42.168 --> 00:01:44.036
actually engage
multiple targets,

00:01:44.136 --> 00:01:45.204
which they do in combat.

00:01:45.270 --> 00:01:46.673
It's not just a one and done.

00:01:46.739 --> 00:01:48.842
Now when you create
that kind of scenario,

00:01:48.908 --> 00:01:52.011
it allows me to truly test
the balance of the weapon.

00:01:52.111 --> 00:01:53.613
When I say "balance,"
it's not only

00:01:53.679 --> 00:01:55.882
just the weapon in my hand,
it's how do I move with my legs

00:01:55.948 --> 00:01:59.018
with it, when I'm moving around
attacking different targets.

00:01:59.118 --> 00:02:01.353
Every time you move,
it really gives you

00:02:01.454 --> 00:02:04.357
information about how
the weight of that weapon

00:02:04.423 --> 00:02:06.158
will affect the way you move.

00:02:06.225 --> 00:02:08.594
This is a multi use
weapon, so I wanted to see

00:02:08.694 --> 00:02:11.063
how many different ways
can I cut, can I thrust,

00:02:11.130 --> 00:02:12.398
can I chop with it.

00:02:15.134 --> 00:02:17.202
Pre-testing the
Joyeuse against a boar

00:02:17.269 --> 00:02:19.372
really gives us
information of that edge,

00:02:19.438 --> 00:02:21.673
how well it can cut thick hide.

00:02:21.774 --> 00:02:23.976
[music playing]

00:02:24.043 --> 00:02:24.943
Sure was a lot of fun.

00:02:25.044 --> 00:02:28.515
[music playing]

00:02:34.187 --> 00:02:35.355
It will kill.

00:02:35.421 --> 00:02:36.555
Good luck, we'll
see you in four days.

00:02:36.656 --> 00:02:39.692 line:14%
[music playing]

00:02:41.761 --> 00:02:44.530
So I'm going to use a big
piece of 5160 bar stock.

00:02:44.596 --> 00:02:47.366
It can take a lot of
damage and flex well.

00:02:47.433 --> 00:02:49.268
I want to make sure I got
the length of the blade

00:02:49.334 --> 00:02:51.938
done down to a reasonable size.

00:02:52.004 --> 00:02:55.007
So this steal is definitely the
most awkward thing that I've

00:02:55.073 --> 00:02:56.375
ever worked with in the shop.

00:02:56.442 --> 00:02:58.144
It's like a big wet noodle.

00:02:58.244 --> 00:03:01.113
I'm going to weld up a
15 layer Damascus fillet

00:03:01.180 --> 00:03:02.882
and make a Swiss
pattern Damascus.

00:03:02.949 --> 00:03:07.053
I think it'll really set the
sword up for a nice look.

00:03:07.119 --> 00:03:08.955
So I got the forge
weld set, and I'm

00:03:09.021 --> 00:03:10.089
going to draw it out to length.

00:03:10.156 --> 00:03:13.593
[music playing]

00:03:14.593 --> 00:03:16.429
Now that I have my
pieces all shaped,

00:03:16.495 --> 00:03:19.432
I'm going to start heat
treating the blade.

00:03:19.532 --> 00:03:22.034
So I get my sword up to
the perfect temperature,

00:03:22.101 --> 00:03:25.371
and I'm ready for quench.

00:03:25.437 --> 00:03:28.907
And I pull it out, and
it's just beautiful.

00:03:28.974 --> 00:03:30.276
[laughs]

00:03:30.376 --> 00:03:34.447
It feels amazing to have
a fully quenched blade.

00:03:34.547 --> 00:03:36.649
So my biggest fear of
putting in this fuller

00:03:36.749 --> 00:03:38.317
is just grinding right
through my blade.

00:03:38.383 --> 00:03:41.087
And I can kind of tell
how close it is just

00:03:41.187 --> 00:03:42.755
by feeling it with my hand.

00:03:42.822 --> 00:03:44.823
After about an hour,
the fuller is done,

00:03:44.923 --> 00:03:47.192
and everything is looking good.

00:03:47.259 --> 00:03:48.594
Coming out pretty well.

00:03:48.695 --> 00:03:51.130
Now I can work on profiling
the pommel and guard

00:03:51.196 --> 00:03:55.401
and getting them exactly
to where I want it.

00:03:55.501 --> 00:03:57.603
For my handle, I
choose diamond wood

00:03:57.670 --> 00:03:59.772
because it can take
a lot of abuse,

00:03:59.839 --> 00:04:00.772
and it's not going to break.

00:04:00.873 --> 00:04:03.776
[music playing]

00:04:03.843 --> 00:04:05.144
I'm in the homestretch now.

00:04:05.211 --> 00:04:08.347 line:14%
It's a good looking piece.

00:04:08.413 --> 00:04:09.949 line:8%
MITCH: We're going to
start out with a bar

00:04:10.016 --> 00:04:12.085
of 1075 high carbon steel.

00:04:12.151 --> 00:04:14.086
We're going to do a lot
of the quick forging

00:04:14.152 --> 00:04:15.854
to shake with the power hammer.

00:04:15.921 --> 00:04:18.357
Whenever you try to move a
big piece of metal like this,

00:04:18.423 --> 00:04:20.025
it's quite a challenge
to keep it straight.

00:04:20.092 --> 00:04:21.894
[rumbling]

00:04:21.961 --> 00:04:23.262
Whoa.

00:04:23.329 --> 00:04:28.200
It's getting long and
heavy and hard to hold.

00:04:28.300 --> 00:04:30.636
It's cooling down between
a couple of 2 by 6s,

00:04:30.736 --> 00:04:32.905
so that way it doesn't
warp as it cools down.

00:04:33.006 --> 00:04:35.641
Now we're going to get
ready for heat treatment.

00:04:35.742 --> 00:04:37.476
Getting pretty close to
coming up the temperature,

00:04:37.543 --> 00:04:39.912
so we're about
five minutes away,

00:04:39.979 --> 00:04:42.214
and we'll be quenching it.

00:04:42.281 --> 00:04:43.783
This is it.

00:04:46.685 --> 00:04:49.121
And then, my hand
cramps, and I drop

00:04:49.187 --> 00:04:51.957
the blade into the quench tank.

00:04:52.057 --> 00:04:53.526
Well.

00:04:53.626 --> 00:04:55.227
I'm worried about that hitting
the bottom of the quench tank

00:04:55.328 --> 00:04:57.563
did some damage.

00:04:57.664 --> 00:04:58.697
Come on, man.

00:04:58.764 --> 00:05:01.400
I tried to fish it out,
but, unfortunately, I

00:05:01.467 --> 00:05:02.968
didn't catch anything.

00:05:03.035 --> 00:05:05.370
Ended up pouring it out in the
five gallon bucket in my yard.

00:05:05.470 --> 00:05:08.574
I got the blade out,
so it's all good now.

00:05:08.641 --> 00:05:11.810
I did pick up a slight
warp close to the tip.

00:05:11.877 --> 00:05:13.413
I should be able to
straighten that out there

00:05:13.513 --> 00:05:14.880
in the temper cycle.

00:05:14.980 --> 00:05:17.516
So time will tell.

00:05:17.616 --> 00:05:20.186
My biggest focus is going to
be getting the blade straight,

00:05:20.253 --> 00:05:23.589
and so I want to get that out of
the way and then go from there.

00:05:23.656 --> 00:05:26.826
My solution is to extend
the width of the jowls

00:05:26.892 --> 00:05:29.328
with some angle iron,
heat it up, and use

00:05:29.395 --> 00:05:31.797
some wooden dowels to
put the proper pressure

00:05:31.897 --> 00:05:34.166
where it needs to be.

00:05:34.233 --> 00:05:35.434
She's straight.

00:05:35.500 --> 00:05:37.036
Oh, that's so freaking awesome.

00:05:37.102 --> 00:05:38.837
Now I need to make the handle.

00:05:38.938 --> 00:05:41.873
Time's running out, so
it's a race to the finish.

00:05:41.974 --> 00:05:45.445
[music playing]

00:05:46.946 --> 00:05:47.879
She's getting there.

00:05:47.980 --> 00:05:49.248
End of day 4.

00:05:49.348 --> 00:05:51.550
Man, it's been quite a trip.

00:05:51.617 --> 00:05:54.286
Everything turned out
great, a lot of hard work.

00:05:54.386 --> 00:05:57.256
But I believe it really
paid off in the end.

00:05:57.323 --> 00:06:00.325
[laughs] That's a
sword in four days.

00:06:00.426 --> 00:06:04.596
All right, bladesmiths,
welcome to the kill test.

00:06:04.697 --> 00:06:06.365
To find out how lethal
your weapons are according

00:06:06.432 --> 00:06:07.867
to its historic design,
I will take your weapon

00:06:07.933 --> 00:06:10.068
to deliver some killing
slashes and thrusts

00:06:10.135 --> 00:06:11.837
on this poor carcass.

00:06:11.937 --> 00:06:13.773
Mitch, you're up first,
you ready for this?

00:06:13.873 --> 00:06:14.773
Yes, sir.

00:06:14.874 --> 00:06:17.910
[music playing]

00:06:33.592 --> 00:06:34.526
All right, Mitch.

00:06:34.593 --> 00:06:36.862
Let's talk about
your sword here.

00:06:36.929 --> 00:06:40.199
Your edge coupled with a
weight that you have here

00:06:40.299 --> 00:06:43.468
allows for very deep
cuts with every strike.

00:06:43.535 --> 00:06:46.905
Overall, sir, it will kill.

00:06:46.972 --> 00:06:48.074
Thank you.

00:06:48.141 --> 00:06:49.174
All right, Peyton,
it's your turn.

00:06:49.241 --> 00:06:50.609
You ready?
- Oh, yeah.

00:06:50.676 --> 00:06:52.645
For this test, I'm
not too nervous.

00:06:52.711 --> 00:06:54.780
I'm just excited to see
it happen, honestly.

00:06:54.881 --> 00:06:57.983
I get to see this bore get
cut in half, hopefully.

00:06:58.050 --> 00:07:01.521
[music playing]

00:07:23.141 --> 00:07:24.409
All right, Peyton.

00:07:24.509 --> 00:07:26.779
That was Joyeuse.

00:07:26.846 --> 00:07:28.381
What I like about
this sword, it's

00:07:28.447 --> 00:07:30.349
not just about the
edge or the point,

00:07:30.416 --> 00:07:31.784
it's the balance of this.

00:07:31.884 --> 00:07:36.956
I can actually use some
velocity, and it cuts deep.

00:07:37.056 --> 00:07:39.224
Overall, sir, it will kill.

00:07:39.291 --> 00:07:40.125
Thank you.

00:07:40.226 --> 00:07:43.696
[music playing]

00:07:45.197 --> 00:07:47.432
All right, gentlemen, it's
time for the strength test.

00:07:47.533 --> 00:07:49.735
Now, to test the strength
and overall construction

00:07:49.801 --> 00:07:51.637
of your blades, I
will be attacking

00:07:51.704 --> 00:07:54.073
our armored knights here.

00:07:54.140 --> 00:07:56.542
Now this is not about
what your blades are going

00:07:56.642 --> 00:07:58.477
to do to that target,
but what the target's

00:07:58.577 --> 00:07:59.779
going to do to your blades.

00:07:59.845 --> 00:08:01.179
Mitch, you're up first.
You ready for this?

00:08:01.246 --> 00:08:03.082
- Yes, sir.
- OK.

00:08:03.149 --> 00:08:04.083
Please don't break.

00:08:04.150 --> 00:08:05.016
Please don't break.

00:08:05.117 --> 00:08:08.621
[music playing]

00:08:19.397 --> 00:08:22.234
I think I just peed a little.

00:08:22.334 --> 00:08:23.436
All right, Mitch.

00:08:23.502 --> 00:08:25.438
Your edge did take
some damage here.

00:08:25.505 --> 00:08:29.074
You can see the chip right
there and some rolls.

00:08:29.141 --> 00:08:30.643
And your sword is heavy.

00:08:30.709 --> 00:08:34.113
You know, this is a lot of
weight for a single handed

00:08:34.213 --> 00:08:36.281
sword, more in the range
of a two handed sword

00:08:36.348 --> 00:08:37.182
as far as the weight goes.

00:08:37.283 --> 00:08:39.184
But she held up.

00:08:39.251 --> 00:08:41.287
She's in one piece.

00:08:41.354 --> 00:08:42.287
Good job, Mitch.

00:08:42.354 --> 00:08:43.522
Thank you.

00:08:43.622 --> 00:08:44.790
All right, Peyton, you're up.

00:08:44.891 --> 00:08:45.858
You're ready?

00:08:45.925 --> 00:08:47.426
Yeah.
[laughs]

00:08:47.526 --> 00:08:48.560
One of those I
don't know which

00:08:48.661 --> 00:08:49.928
way my head's going to go?
Yeah.

00:08:50.029 --> 00:08:53.599
[music playing]

00:09:12.250 --> 00:09:13.585
All right, Peyton.

00:09:13.652 --> 00:09:16.021
It's weighty, but the weight
is all back in my hands,

00:09:16.121 --> 00:09:19.691
so it doesn't feel as
heavy in the blade.

00:09:19.758 --> 00:09:21.627
This sword has a much
better point of balance

00:09:21.727 --> 00:09:23.028
than the other sword.

00:09:23.128 --> 00:09:25.564
Your blade did take some
chips and some edge rolling.

00:09:25.630 --> 00:09:28.000
But I think your
grinds are beautiful.

00:09:28.067 --> 00:09:30.436
The sword is all solid.

00:09:30.503 --> 00:09:31.837
You did a good job.

00:09:31.937 --> 00:09:32.838
Thank you.

00:09:32.939 --> 00:09:35.841
[music playing]

00:09:37.510 --> 00:09:40.112
All right, bladesmiths,
welcome to the sharpness

00:09:40.179 --> 00:09:43.115
test, the sandbag gauntlet.

00:09:43.182 --> 00:09:45.183
Now, to test the
sharpness of your weapon,

00:09:45.283 --> 00:09:46.718
I will slash across these bags.

00:09:46.818 --> 00:09:48.687
Now, unlike the strength test,
this is all about how sharp

00:09:48.788 --> 00:09:50.923
your blades are and how
well they cut these bags.

00:09:50.990 --> 00:09:52.391
Mitch, you're up first.
You ready?

00:09:52.491 --> 00:09:53.391
Yes, sir.

00:09:53.492 --> 00:09:56.729
[music playing]

00:10:10.142 --> 00:10:11.210
All right, Mitch.

00:10:11.277 --> 00:10:13.212
So despite some of the
damage of rolls and chips,

00:10:13.279 --> 00:10:15.914
it wasn't an issue at all
in cutting these bags.

00:10:16.014 --> 00:10:16.982
It will cut.

00:10:17.049 --> 00:10:17.883
Thank you.

00:10:17.950 --> 00:10:19.251
All right, Peyton,
your turn, sir.

00:10:19.317 --> 00:10:20.452
Are you ready?
- Yes, sir.

00:10:20.519 --> 00:10:24.090
[music playing]

00:10:39.071 --> 00:10:40.105
All right, Peyton.

00:10:40.205 --> 00:10:42.408
The handle construction
is smooth but ovoid

00:10:42.508 --> 00:10:43.842
enough to where I
wrap my hand around it

00:10:43.909 --> 00:10:45.344
and I get a very good grip.

00:10:45.444 --> 00:10:46.411
It will cut.

00:10:46.478 --> 00:10:48.714
Thank you.

00:10:48.780 --> 00:10:51.249
Mitch, Peyton, the judge's
deliberation is complete.

00:10:51.349 --> 00:10:54.320
You guys have done fantastic
work on these finale weapons,

00:10:54.386 --> 00:10:57.422
but there can only be one
"Forged in Fire" champion.

00:10:57.522 --> 00:11:02.428
The new "Forged in
Fire" champion is

00:11:02.528 --> 00:11:05.064
Peyton, congratulations, you're
the "Forged in Fire" champion.

00:11:05.130 --> 00:11:08.267
Mitch, unfortunately, your
blade didn't make the cut.

00:11:08.334 --> 00:11:10.736
Mitch, you brought us a
sword that performed well

00:11:10.836 --> 00:11:13.472
in all three of our tests, so
this came down to the finer

00:11:13.572 --> 00:11:15.607
points of craftsmanship
as in where

00:11:15.674 --> 00:11:17.509
to place the balance
point on that blade

00:11:17.576 --> 00:11:19.144
and the general weight.

00:11:19.211 --> 00:11:21.513
That balance point being so far
forward made it harder to wield

00:11:21.580 --> 00:11:22.714
and harder to
control, and that's

00:11:22.781 --> 00:11:24.082
why we're letting you go.

00:11:24.183 --> 00:11:25.084
I understand.

00:11:25.150 --> 00:11:26.618
Mitch, you've been
a great competitor

00:11:26.718 --> 00:11:28.621
of this entire competition,
but at this time,

00:11:28.721 --> 00:11:31.990
I have to ask you to please
surrender your blade.

00:11:32.090 --> 00:11:33.459
MITCH: Obviously, a
little disappointed.

00:11:33.526 --> 00:11:35.661
Overall, happy with
what I turned in,

00:11:35.728 --> 00:11:37.196
and I'm happy for Peyton.

00:11:37.296 --> 00:11:39.531
If I had to lose to anyone,
I'd just sooner lose to him.

00:11:39.598 --> 00:11:42.300
[music playing]

00:11:42.367 --> 00:11:45.637
Peyton, congratulations, you
are the new "Forged in Fire"

00:11:45.704 --> 00:11:47.273
champion, and that
is a title that

00:11:47.339 --> 00:11:50.075
comes with a check for $10,000.

00:11:50.142 --> 00:11:51.143
Congratulations.

00:11:51.243 --> 00:11:54.580
Please present your
sword to the judges.

00:11:54.680 --> 00:11:56.648
I'm the next "Forged
in Fire" champion.

00:11:56.749 --> 00:11:58.250
It's just crazy.

00:11:58.350 --> 00:12:00.085
As soon as I heard my name,
it's just like a weight just got

00:12:00.186 --> 00:12:03.756
pulled off my chest, just
like [sighs] it's over.

00:12:03.822 --> 00:12:06.124
[laughs] Finally I can breathe.

00:12:06.225 --> 00:12:09.729
[music playing]

